WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.290
A bag of sweets at lunchtime.

2
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.350
A skipped meal at teatime.

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.330
The glucose in your blood ought
to swing wildly up and down.

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.870
Yet all day, it stays
inside a narrow range.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.910
So what is holding it steady?

6
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.270
In this mission, you'll find out
how the pancreas monitors the

7
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.990
glucose in your blood, and
releases a hormone called insulin.

8
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.550
You'll see how the liver can
store spare glucose as glycogen.

9
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.370
And you'll meet negative feedback,

10
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.790
and find out what goes
wrong in diabetes.

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.990
Your mission: discover what
keeps your blood glucose steady.
